{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the earth.</b> He now mentions <b>Elohim</b> to invoke upon them the attribute of justice, for it is drawn taut against them because of their great sin." "And it says <b>and behold it was corrupted</b> — and what is the corruption? That ״all flesh had corrupted its way.״ He called them all by the name 'flesh' because all of them were corrupters of the seed, in the manner of what is written (Isaiah 27): ״שוחטי הילדים״ — and our Sages of blessed memory interpreted: do not read שוחטי (slaughterers) but סוחטי (crushers). And because they corrupted the seed of man, which is formed in forty days, therefore their punishment was measure for measure: to be destroyed by the waters of the flood, which came down upon them forty days. Four transgressions were among them: idolatry, illicit relations, bloodshed, and robbery. And the reason for the forty: each and every one corresponds to the fact that they would worship the sun thirty days, and the sun's power operates upon it five days before its arrival in its nullity, and five days after it departs from its nullity — and so there are forty days during which the sun and its forces stand in nullity, forty days; and likewise for each and every constellation, forty days. This corresponds to idolatry, illicit relations, and bloodshed. And the robbery: because its perpetrators transgress the laws of the Torah, which was given in forty days. And the sin of this corruption was not among the children of man alone, but among all other living creatures. And so our Sages of blessed memory interpreted: ברותחין קלקלו וברותחין נדונו — with boiling waters they corrupted and with boiling waters they were judged, for the waters of the flood were boiling. It is written here: ״וישכו המים״ — and it is written there (Esther 7:10): ״וחמת המלך שככה״. And what he mentioned, ״ותשחת הארץ לפני האלהים״ — this is the corruption of idolatry. And Scripture hints to you that they were wicked and sinful in transgressions between man and the Place, such as the corruption of idolatry and the corruption of the seed, and also in transgressions between man and his fellow, such as robbery — each and every one was robbing and extorting from the other, as it says: ״ותמלא הארץ חמס״. And from the fact that he mentioned a second time that ״the earth was filled with robbery because of them,״ and mentioned upon this ״קץ כל בשר בא לפני״ — the end of all flesh has come before Me — Scripture explains to you that the decree was sealed upon them only because of robbery. And so Isaiah said, peace be upon him (Isaiah 54:14): ״רחקי מעושק כי לא תיראי וממחת כי לא תקרב אליך״. And he mentioned above (ibid. v. 9): ״כי מי נח זאת לי״ — for this is to Me as the waters of Noah — for he warns about the great sin on account of which the destruction of the generation of the flood drew near. And the reason is that robbery is among the rationally perceived commandments, such that even had the Torah not been given, a person would derive them through his reason; and the first rational perception is that a person has no claim whatsoever to his fellow's property." "<b>And know</b> that the matter of the flood is clear proof of the creation of the world and of divine providence, when we see that the Holy One, blessed be He, punishes and annihilates the wicked from the world and leaves a remnant of the righteous, such as Noah and his sons — this is a sign that the world is created and that providence flows down to the lowly. For surely, just as the first man was father and head to all creatures after him, so was Noah father and head to all creatures after the flood; and just as the first man had three sons — Cain, Abel, Seth — of whom two were principal and one was cursed, so you find with Noah three sons — Shem, Ham, and Japheth — of whom two were principal and one was cursed; and just as you find with the third son of the first man, Seth, that through him the world was perpetuated and he was the principal of the sons, so with the sons of Noah you find the third one the principal of the sons, and that is Shem, for no nation merits the revival of the dead except the sons of Shem."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:57.449171593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}